-- CA_0161_la_elem_high_trustee_areas.sql
-- Give the 22 LA-County elementary and high-school boards that elect BY TRUSTEE AREA their area geography,
-- and move each seat onto its area, so an address sees its own trustee (plus any at-large holdover) instead
-- of the whole board. Follows CA_0158 (which seated the verified boards on the whole-district rows) and the
-- unified trustee-area batches (CA_0144-CA_0154). CA_0162 seeds the Nov 3 2026 races on these seats.
--
--   Antelope Valley JUHSD 0602820  Castaic 0607740 (areas A-E)  Centinela Valley UHSD 0607920
--   East Whittier City 0611850     Eastside Union 0611910       El Monte UHSD 0612120
--   Garvey 0614940                 Hughes-Elizabeth Lakes 0617880  Keppel Union 0619440 (transition)
--   Lancaster 0620880              Lawndale 0621210             Little Lake City 0621930
--   Los Nietos 0622890             Newhall 0627180              Palmdale 0629580 (transition)
--   Saugus Union 0635970           South Whittier 0637560       Sulphur Springs Union 0638220
--   Whittier City 0642450          Whittier UHSD 0642480        William S. Hart UHSD 0642510
--   Wilsona 0642810
-- The 9 at-large boards (Westside, Gorman, Hawthorne, Hermosa Beach, Lennox, El Monte City, Mountain View,
-- Rosemead, Valle Lindo) are unchanged.
--
-- No migration runner exists; this file records SQL applied by hand (pure DML).
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A. THE POLYGONS -- one per trustee area, mtfcc X0002 (the school sub-district layer the lookup join admits)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Dissolved from the LA County Registrar-Recorder precinct layer (public.gis.lacounty.gov
-- .../Political_Boundaries/MapServer/34, read 2026-09-22) -- the geography the Registrar uses to put each
-- "Trustee Area No. N" contest on a ballot. Elementary districts use DST_ESD/DIV_ESD, high-school districts
-- DST_HSD/DIV_HSD. Codes decoded by point-in-polygon of 33,236 precinct points against each district's own
-- TIGER polygon (G5400 / G5410), >= 99% agreement per code:
--   ESD 36 Lawndale, 46 Garvey, 52 Eastside, 54 Hughes-Elizabeth Lakes, 55 Keppel, 56 Lancaster, 57 Palmdale,
--   60 Wilsona, 61 Castaic, 62 Newhall, 63 Saugus, 64 Sulphur Springs, 71 East Whittier, 72 Little Lake,
--   73 Los Nietos, 74 South Whittier, 75 Whittier City; HSD 35 Centinela Valley, 52 Antelope Valley,
--   61 Hart, 65 El Monte UHSD, 71 Whittier UHSD.
-- Every district dissolves into exactly five divisions 1-5. The union of each district's areas covers
-- 96.9-100% of its TIGER polygon with <= 0.8% outside it -- except LANCASTER (94%): the Registrar codes
-- ~13 km2 of TIGER's Lancaster polygon to another elementary district (ESD 59), so its tolerance is 7%.
-- CASTAIC's areas are lettered: division 1-5 = A-E. The Registrar and the county trustee-area layer store
-- them by number only; the district's own board-adopted map ("Red II", NDC, 2017-02-16, linked from
-- castaicusd.com "By-Trustee Area Boundary Map") shows A = the large western area (division 1, 273 km2),
-- B = the small northern area by Castaic Lagoon (2, 2.6 km2), C = central (3, 6.3 km2), D = east (4, 75 km2),
-- E = south (5, 50 km2) -- the same order (A = 1) as Glendale and Torrance (CA_0150 / CA_0153).
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- B. THE SEATS
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Each area gets one SCHOOL sub-district (geo_id '<district>-ta-<n>', mtfcc X0002). The office each
-- verified member holds (CA_0158) moves onto that member's area, titled 'Board Member (Trustee Area N)';
-- the member's term is untouched. Member-to-area comes from each district's board page (research of
-- 2026-09-22, CA_0158) cross-checked with the RR/CC contest each member won. 103 areas carry a member.
--   * LITTLE LAKE TA5 is vacant (Gina Almanza-Ramirez resigned 2026-05-11; CA_0158 vacated it): its office
--     moves to area 5 and stays vacant; its remainder is on the Nov 2026 ballot.
--   * PALMDALE and KEPPEL are MID-TRANSITION (the CA_0152 / Montebello model, decision 2026-09-22): the
--     three members elected AT LARGE in Nov 2022 (Palmdale: Nancy Smith, Ralph Velador, Simone Zulu Diol;
--     Keppel: Blanca Nava, Andrew Ramirez, Alma Rodriguez) represent the whole district until Dec 2026, so
--     their offices STAY on the whole-district row, titled 'Board Member (At-Large)'. Their 2024 members sit
--     by area (Palmdale TA2 Vega, TA4 Hunt; Keppel TA4 Klee, TA5 Teff). The areas first filled by the Nov 2026
--     election (Palmdale TA1, TA3, TA5; Keppel TA1, TA2, TA3 -- the RR/CC 2026 contests) get a NEW office,
--     copied from a sibling seat and flagged vacant (vacant_since NULL, the date is not a vacancy), to carry
--     their race. offices_missing_terms rises by these 6 flagged-vacant seats only.
--
-- ROLLBACK: move each office in _ta (kind member/vacant) back to its parent district row and title
--   'Board Member'; DELETE the 6 fresh offices (_ta kind 'fresh'); retitle the 6 _hold offices 'Board
--   Member'; DELETE the 110 districts and 110 X0002 geofence_boundaries whose geo_id is in _ta.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: polygons, districts and offices are inserted only where absent; each office moves only while
-- it is still on its parent row; retitles are guarded on the title. A re-run is a no-op and the gate passes.
-- ===================================================================================================

BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE _ta (parent_geo text, geo_id text, label text, ta text, kind text, office_id uuid, holder_pid uuid, holder_name text, template_office uuid, tol float8, gj text) ON COMMIT DROP;
